{"id":"d5a1c7eab66450b265912b15da03172ebd5547e02cc74dcaf0409cb418b4cf84","lamport":0,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.100548Z","format_version":1,"kind":"create","payload":{"fields":{"created-at":"2026-10-04T12:18:03.100548Z","created-by":"carlo.cifarelli@gmail.com","description":"Low-risk de-risking step 2/6 of the op-log roadmap (parent 0e7b1245).\n\nAdd a format-version key per ticket plus a `ti migrate` command so incompatible\nformat changes are survivable for existing repos. Must land before the op-log\nformat break so the flagship migration has a vehicle.","parent":"0e7b1245-e860-4843-9df3-101cd9a0a746","priority":"3","spec":"# Spec — Format versioning per ticket + `ti migrate`\n\nRoadmap step 2/6 (parent 0e7b12). Low-risk; makes the op-log format break survivable.\n\n## Goal\n\nGive each ticket a declared format version and ship a `ti migrate` command so an\nincompatible layout change (notably step 4's op-log) can be rolled forward on\nexisting repos without data loss, and so older binaries fail loudly rather than\nsilently misreading new data.\n\n## Current state (precedent already exists)\n\n- `keys.rs` has a GLOBAL `ticgit:schema-version` key (`SCHEMA_VERSION = \"1\"`),\n  seeded by `store.rs::ensure_schema` and read by `TicketStore::schema_version`.\n- `store.rs::build_ticket` ALREADY performs an implicit migration: it folds\n  legacy `state` values (`hold` → Blocked, `open` → New, `resolved`/`invalid` →\n  closed states) into the current split status/state model. This is the pattern\n  to formalize.\n\n## Design\n\n- Add a per-ticket version field: `keys::ticket_field(id, \"format-version\")`\n  (helper + `parse` support in `keys.rs`). Absent = implicit \"1\" (legacy).\n- Bump the global `SCHEMA_VERSION` only on layout-wide breaks; use the per-ticket\n  version for per-ticket rolling migration so a large repo migrates incrementally\n  (and partial migration is safe — unmigrated tickets still read).\n- `ti migrate` command (`commands/migrate.rs`):\n  - dry-run by default (`--write` to apply), prints a per-ticket from→to plan.\n  - idempotent: re-running on an already-current ticket is a no-op.\n  - each migration is a pure function `migrate_vN_to_vN+1(fields) -> fields`,\n    registered in a table so steps chain (v1→v2→v3).\n  - reuses the `build_ticket` legacy-folding logic as the v0→v1 migration,\n    formalizing today's implicit behavior.\n- Read path: `build_ticket` checks `format-version`; if below the binary's max,\n  apply migrations in memory (lazy read-time migration) so reads never break even\n  before `ti migrate --write` is run. `--write` just persists the lazy result.\n- Version-too-new guard: if a ticket's `format-version` exceeds what this binary\n  knows, refuse with a clear \"upgrade `ti`\" error instead of corrupting it.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `keys.rs`: `format-version` field helper.\n- `store.rs`: version-aware `build_ticket`; migration registry; `set_format_version`.\n- `commands/migrate.rs` + wire into `cli.rs`; `--json`/`--markdown` per the\n  machine-output contract (plan as structured output; diagnostics to stderr).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- CLI test: a repo seeded with legacy `state: hold` reads correctly and\n  `ti migrate --write` upgrades it; second run is a no-op.\n- CLI test: a ticket with a future `format-version` fails non-zero with guidance.\n- `--json` migrate plan is valid JSON on stdout, no ANSI.\n\n## Risks\n\n- Must land BEFORE step 4 so the op-log introduction is itself a versioned\n  migration, not an unversioned break.","state":"review","status":"open","title":"Format versioning per ticket + ti migrate"}}}